      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject ID: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- term code '2022FA': COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- offering department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- offering school name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\n- number of unique subjects: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- average number of enrolled students: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- course material status 'RQ': TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA', show the subject ID, department name, term description, and the running sum of total units within each academic year, ordered by subject ID.\n```sql\nSELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.TERM_DESCRIPTION, SUM(t1.TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL t0 JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.TERM_CODE = '2022FA'\n```\n2. For each offering department and school where the course material status is 'RQ', provide the number of unique subjects and the minimum total units for those subjects.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ' GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME;\n```\n3. For subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA', show the subject ID, department name, term description, and the running sum of total units within each academic year, along with the offering department name, offering school name, the number of unique subjects, and the minimum total units for each offering department and school where the course material status is 'RQ', ordered by subject ID.\n```sql\nWITH subq1 AS ( SELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.TERM_DESCRIPTION, SUM(t1.TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column, t1.TERM_CODE FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL t0 JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.TERM_CODE = '2022FA' ), subq2 AS ( SELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ' GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME ) SELECT s1.SUBJECT_ID, s1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, s1.window_column, s2.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s2.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, s2.subject_count, s2.min_total_units FROM subq1 s1 JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso ON s1.SUBJECT_ID = tso.SUBJECT_ID AND s1.TERM_CODE = tso.TERM_CODE JOIN subq2 s2 ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = s2.OFFER_DEPT_NAME AND tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME = s2.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME ORDER BY s1.SUBJECT_ID\n```\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA', show the subject ID, department name, term description, and the running sum of total units within each academic year, along with the offering department name, offering school name, the number of unique subjects, the minimum total units, and the average number of enrolled students for each offering department and school where the course material status is 'RQ', ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers."
